    "created_at": "2023-10-09T04:54:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-09T04:54:39Z",
    "body": "That's not the concern, actually. The issue is that several of these features run in browser processes (usually the network process) which don't have a JavaScript engine, and thus don't have a regular expression engine. Bringing regexp support to the network process would require bringing a whole copy of V8, which as you can imagine, is not trivial.\r\n\r\n(I'll also note that browser security doesn't make a distinction of the sort you're discussing, between \"dangerous\" untrusted input and \"non-dangerous\" untrusted input. Any untrusted input at all falls afoul of [the rule of 2](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/master/docs/security/rule-of-2.md), at least in Chromium.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/urlpattern/issues/comments/1752345633/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
