    "created_at": "2023-10-09T06:45:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-09T06:45:30Z",
    "body": "This concern applies to server operators too, e.g., with compression dictionaries. This again leads me to think that having some kind of subset would be a good idea.\r\n\r\nIt seems like another way of stating the constraint here is that there's no interest in implementing a regular expression engine in a safe language.",
