    "created_at": "2023-10-27T01:25:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-10-27T01:25:47Z",
    "body": "Anyone want to bikeshed the name here? I think we should use \"`RegExp`\" (instead of e.g. `Regex`) since that's what JavaScript uses. With that as a base, some ideas so far:\r\n\r\n- `hasRegExpTokens` / `hasRegExpGroups`\r\n- `containsRegExpTokens` / `containsRegExpGroups`\r\n- `requiresRegExp`\r\n- `usesRegExp`",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
